<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Celesc cut to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Celesc cut to hold.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresdner Kleinwort Benson analyst Cecilia Tam said Thursday she had cut her rating for Brazilian power company Centrais Eletricas de Santa Catarina SA, or Celesc, to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Although we continue to believe that Celesc holds one of the best concessions in Brazil, the sharp increase in its share price over the last year and the lower probability of an early privatization cause us to believe that Celesc has reached fair value,&quot; Tam wrote in an analysis.</p>
<p>-- &quot;... As a state-owned utility, Celesc should continue to face difficulties cutting costs.&quot;</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
